{%- comment -%}
  PG R36H Pro Tiles (2026-09-16): the R36H Pro page's offer tiles, in the same
  design as the R36S page's Single / Duo Pack / Trio Pack tiles, with the
  orb page's image dropdowns (window.pgDrop, pg-theme-css) for the colour
  pickers.

  Registered in templates/product.pg-r36h.json only. The R36S page's tiles are
  built by pgDuo (pg-theme-css) from two separate pack PRODUCTS and are hard
  wired to the handheld-game-console handle. This product carries every offer
  as its own VARIANT (Bundle x Color x Second Console Color), so the tiles here
  are rendered from the product's variants in Liquid, and Add to cart posts the
  exact variant the shopper configured. Nothing is computed at checkout, so the
  cart charges what the tile prints.

  THE MARKUP IS THE PACK TILES' MARKUP (.pgx-tile.pgx-duo, .pgx-duo-head,
  .pgx-duo-t, .pgx-duo-px, .pgx-lad-badge, .pgx-lad-chip, .pgx-tier-note) and
  the ladder tiles' picker block (.pgx-lad-picks > .lbl + .pgx-lad-row, one
  pgDrop per console), so pg-theme-css, pg-dark, pg-save-badge, pg-pick-size
  and pg-r36s-mobile style and behave on these exactly as they do on the R36S
  and the orb: dark tile, purple SAVE pill on the top edge, the picker block
  that opens on the selected tile, the tier note under it, the in-tile ADD TO
  CART on phones.

  WHAT IS STOOD DOWN ON THIS PAGE, AND WHY:
    - pgLadder (pg-theme-css) builds a Buy 2 Get 1 ladder on every product it
      does not list by name; that ladder mirrors discounts this product does
      not carry. window.pgLadder is claimed here first (this section renders
      in the template, the footer group after it), so its guard returns.
    - pgDuo (pg-theme-css) would only decorate the first native tile and add a
      SAVE pill computed from the first variant. Claimed the same way.
    - pg-landing's own Single tile ([data-pgx-tile="single"]) is hidden by CSS
      and its #pgx-atc handler never runs: the window-capture listener below
      takes every Add to cart click first, the same mechanism pg-r36s-mobile
      uses for the pack tiles.
    - pg-tile-copy's generic .pgx-deal-note is hidden by the same
      data-pg-tiernotes flag pgDuo sets on the R36S; each tile carries its own
      note instead.

  THE SINGLE DEVICE CAN BE BOUGHT AS A PAIR (2026-09-17, by request: "for the
  single bundle add option for duo pack ... they can choose color too ... it
  should auto change within that tile ... the wording should change
  accordingly"). The Single Device tile carries a two-way switch, 1 Console /
  Duo Pack. On Duo Pack the tile renames itself (Duo Pack, 2x 64GB, "15,000+
  games each"), a second colour picker appears and the tags read Console 1
  / Console 2, and the price, the struck price, the SAVE pill and the note
  under the pickers all follow.
  THE DUO PACK IS $5.00 OFF EACH CONSOLE, AND THE TILL DOES IT (2026-09-17). It
  was first priced as two singles, $149.98 against $199.98, the same 25% the
  single shows. The owner then asked for 30% off and chose, asked directly,
  "$139.98 for two": 30% under the $199.98 the two are struck at, the same
  measure every SAVE pill on this page uses. There is still no Duo variant.
  The admin carries an automatic discount, "R36H Pro - Duo Pack Savings":
  $5.00 off each Single Device (64GB) variant, minimum quantity 2, applies to
  each item, combines with order, product and shipping discounts (the same
  shape as the DBZ lamp packs, and the Extra 5% stacks on it). Add to cart
  posts the two Single Device variants that were picked (one line of two when
  the colours match) and checkout takes the $10.00 off, so fulfilment is
  untouched. THE TILE MIRRORS THAT DISCOUNT, IT DOES NOT MAKE IT: the amount
  is the section setting "duo_off" (5.00). Change the discount in the admin
  and this setting together, or the tile prints a price the till will not
  charge. pg-cart-addons reads the same discount off /cart.js for its
  upgrade button.
  A "30% off" pill at the OLD price was asked about first and not built:
  $149.98 is 25% under $199.98, so it would have needed a struck price the
  consoles were never sold at.
  tilePaint (pg-theme-css) stamps color:#fff !important inline on everything
  inside a tile, so the switch is drawn in white type and its quiet second
  line is dimmed with opacity, not with a colour.

  ONE LINE PER PICKER, AND NO "CHOOSE YOUR COLOR" (2026-09-17, by report on the
  Duo Pack: "there is text wrapping ... console 1 and console 2 just looks
  crammed and weird, I don't know if you need to say choose your color").
    - the line under the tile's name is short enough to stay on one line at
      360px with the wider two-console price beside it ("15,000+ games
      each"; the name and the 2x chip already say there are two);
    - the label over the pickers is gone from all three tiles. Each picker
      carries its own tag instead: "Color" for one console, "Console 1" and
      "Console 2" for two;
    - on a phone pg-pick-size stacks a picker row (tag centred above a
      full-width picker), which is what read as crammed with two of them.
      Here the tag sits to the LEFT of its picker on one line, the way the
      row is drawn on desktop.

  THE DUO MAX BUNDLE NAMES ITS ACCESSORIES BEFORE IT IS OPENED (2026-09-17, by
  request: "should say the 4 accessories but like 2x so people know before
  they click on the bundle, in that purple"). The Max Bundle's chip says
  "+ 4 Accessories"; the Duo Max only said "2x 128GB, 20K Games", and its
  doubled kit was listed only once the tile was selected. It carries a second
  purple chip, "2x 4 Accessories". Two chips, not one longer one: a chip does
  not wrap (white-space:nowrap, width:max-content from pg-case-mobile), and
  "2x 128GB, 20K Games + 2x 4 Accessories" in one chip runs under the price
  on anything narrower than about 430px.
  Its line under the chips said "Two consoles, one price". It reads like the
  Max Bundle's now (2026-09-17, by request: "take out the 2 console one price
  thing ... say something similar to the one above it"): "Two consoles, two
  protection kits", after the Max's "Console plus the full protection kit",
  and short enough to stay on one line at 440px beside the wider price.

  A LARGER "128GB" CHIP ON THE MAX TILES WAS TRIED AND TAKEN BACK OUT
  (2026-09-17: asked for as "128gb is main selling point of the max bundles",
  then "no i dont like what you did to the bundles for the 128gb"). The Max
  tiles are as they were: one chip that opens with 128GB.
  NO PER CONSOLE PRICE IN THE DUO PACK NOTE (same day: "take out the 69.99
  each in the duo thing"). The note says what is in the pack; the price is the
  tile's own price and the "2 for" line on the switch.
  THE PICKER SITS NEXT TO ITS TAG (same day: "the one console should be closer
  to the color words"). The tags had one fixed width sized for "Console 1", so
  the short word "Color" stood 40px away from its picker. Tags are as wide as
  their word; only the two-console rows share a width, so their pickers line
  up.

  THE PICKERS are built in JS once window.pgDrop exists (pg-theme-css runs
  after this section, in the footer group). If it never appears, a native
  <select> with the same pgValue() interface is used instead, so the page
  still sells.

  ONE SKU PER CART LINE (2026-09-21, AutoDS: "anything that comes with a kit
  or duo pack all needs to be separate line items, and if it's a duo pack
  split the price between the 2"). The Duo Max VARIANTS are gone: the Duo
  Max tile posts two Max Bundle consoles (one per picked colour) and the
  admin's "R36H Pro - Duo Max Savings" takes $30.00 off each from two up
  (the tile mirrors it through duomax_off). The Max and the Duo Max post
  the Protection Kit (r36h-max-kit: silicone daily case, hard shell travel
  case, screen protector as ONE product, the way the supplier ships them)
  as a line of its own, one per console, and "R36H Pro - Max Kit Free" makes it
  free beside a Max console, so the console line carries the whole price
  and the kit row reads FREE. The three add-on products stay separate
  items: they are only sold one at a time under the Single Device.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign p = product -%}
{%- comment -%} the three add-ons sold under the Single Device (2026-09-19, "add
  the same upsells for r36 that you have for the flip ... also screen
  protectors for both, 9.99, 14.99 originally"): one-variant products, read
  live so a reprice in the admin follows on its own {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign add_sil = all_products['r36h-silicone-case'] -%}
{%- assign add_hard = all_products['r36h-hard-shell-travel-case'] -%}
{%- assign add_prot = all_products['r36h-screen-protector'] -%}
{%- comment -%} the Protection Kit (2026-09-21): the three accessories as ONE product, the way the supplier ships them; the Max and Duo Max post it as a line of its own {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign add_kit = all_products['r36h-max-kit'] -%}
{%- if p and p.variants.size > 0 -%}
{%- assign color_opt = blank -%}
{%- for option in p.options_with_values -%}
  {%- if option.name == 'Color' -%}{%- assign color_opt = option -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
<style>
  /* pg-landing's native single tile: replaced by the tiles below */
  #pgx .pgx-buy > .pgx-tile[data-pgx-tile="single"]{display:none !important}
  #pgx .pgx-tile.pg-rh{cursor:pointer}
  #pgx .pgx-tile.pg-rh .pgx-duo-t b{font-size:17px}
  /* the colour's name on the big photo (2026-09-18, asked for on the Flip SP
     first: "when you scroll through hero images it had the colors labeled ...
     add that to the r36 too"): a pill in the photo's top-left corner naming
     the colour whose render is showing; nothing on the other shots. Top-left,
     clear of the SWIPE counter at the foot. */
  #pgx .pgx-hero{position:relative}
  /* on a phone pg-r36s-mobile hides the hero and turns the thumb strip into
     the swipe carousel (html.pg-r36-gal), so every colour render's SLIDE
     carries its own pill; the hero's pill serves the desktop */
  html.pg-r36-gal #pgx .pgx-thumbs > button{position:relative}
  #pgx .pgx-thumbs > button .pg-rh-hcap{display:none}
  html.pg-r36-gal #pgx .pgx-thumbs > button .pg-rh-hcap.on{display:inline-block}
  /* centred over the top of the photo (owner 2026-09-19: "for the colors over the image center them") */
  /* bigger and a touch higher (owner 2026-09-19: "make it bigger and push it up a tad") */
  #pgx .pg-rh-hcap{position:absolute;left:50%;top:8px;transform:translateX(-50%);z-index:3;display:none;padding:9px 17px;border-radius:999px;white-space:nowrap;
    background:rgba(13,7,20,.74);border:1px solid rgba(199,155,234,.55);color:#fff;
    font-family:'Poppins','Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.05em;line-height:1;
    -webkit-backdrop-filter:blur(6px);backdrop-filter:blur(6px);pointer-events:none}
  #pgx .pg-rh-hcap.on{display:inline-block}
  /* the Duo Max Bundle's two chips share one full-width row under the name
     and the price (2026-09-17, "keep the max duo bundle all in one line"):
     in the name column they stacked, "4 Accessories" wrapping down. The sub
     line follows them, restated here because it left .pgx-duo-t. */
  /* the tiles keep their stacked price column (a one-line head with the struck
     price beside the price was tried on 2026-09-17 and undone the same night:
     "idk what u did to bundles but undo that"). What stays: the Duo's chips on
     one full-width row, the Max's sub line on its own row so it cannot wrap in
     the name column, and the Duo's sub line up in the name column so the two-
     line price column leaves no hole beside a one-line name. */
  /* the Max and Duo tiles carry no sub line under their chips (2026-09-18,
     "I meant these sentences ... undo that"); the Duo's one-line name is
     centred against its two-line price column so nothing gapes beside it */
  /* the Max chip sits at the tile's left edge on its own row like the Duo's
     chips (2026-09-18, "all the way to the left side like duo max bundle has").
     Every head is top-aligned, name and dot on the first line ("they should
     all be positioned the same and look the same"); a centred Duo head was
     tried and rejected ("it's like in the center, it should be up like the
     others"). The pack chip rows are pulled up beside the struck price where
     they fit: the Max's everywhere, the Duo's from 420px (its two chips need
     264px next to the struck price). */
  /* the pack tiles sit closer under the tile above (2026-09-18, "move max
     bundle and duo max bundle up higher"): 18px, the hanging pill clears the box above by 6px */
  #pgx#pgx .pgx-buy > .pgx-tile.pg-rh + .pgx-tile.pg-rh{margin-top:6px !important}
  #pgx .pg-rh .pg-rh-meta{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;gap:6px;margin:7px 0 0}
  /* the Duo's chips hug its name the way the Max's chip does (2026-09-18) */
  #pgx .pg-rh[data-rh="max"] .pg-rh-meta{margin-top:-20px;padding-right:64px}
  /* the sentence under the chip ignores the room kept for the struck price */
  #pgx .pg-rh[data-rh="max"] .pg-rh-meta small{flex-basis:calc(100% + 64px)}
  /* the Single's chip sits on the same kind of row, at the tile's left edge, beside the struck price (2026-09-19, "the purple is indented over to the right while everything else is to the left"); its chips are 150 to 175px, so it fits at every width */
  #pgx .pg-rh[data-rh="single"] .pg-rh-meta{margin-top:-20px;padding-right:64px}
  #pgx .pg-rh[data-rh="single"] .pg-rh-meta small{flex-basis:calc(100% + 64px)}
/* no struck price (an AutoDS push wiped compare-at on 2026-09-22 and the chip rode up over the name): the chip drops under the name instead of hugging the strike line */
#pgx .pg-rh .pgx-duo-head:not(:has(s[data-rh-was]:not(:empty))) + .pg-rh-meta{margin-top:7px;padding-right:0}
  #pgx .pg-rh[data-rh="duo"] .pg-rh-meta{margin-top:5px}
  /* one chip on the Duo since 2026-09-18 ("all that info in one purple line like
     the max has"): 249px, beside the struck price from 400px, under the head below */
  /* the Duo Max chip (266px at 12px) clears the price from 425px (room 273px at 430) */
  @media (min-width:425px){ #pgx .pg-rh[data-rh="duo"] .pg-rh-meta{margin-top:-20px;padding-right:64px} #pgx .pg-rh[data-rh="duo"] .pg-rh-meta small{flex-basis:calc(100% + 64px)} }
  #pgx .pg-rh .pg-rh-meta .pgx-lad-chip{display:inline-block !important;margin:0 !important}
  /* the chips are the Flip SP's size (2026-09-19, "the sizes of the font should
     be the same on r36 and the flip sp"): 12.5px, 12px under 450px, 11.5px
     under 390px. Room beside the struck price on this page: about 215px at
     375, 236 at 393, 273 at 430. The Single's chips (170 to 200px) fit
     everywhere; the Max's (~227px at 12px) from 390px and the Duo Max's
     (~272px) from 450px; below those widths the rows sit under the head. */
  #pgx#pgx .pg-rh .pg-rh-meta .pgx-lad-chip{font-size:12.5px !important}
  @media (max-width:449px){ #pgx#pgx .pg-rh .pg-rh-meta .pgx-lad-chip{font-size:12px !important;letter-spacing:0 !important;padding-left:8px !important;padding-right:8px !important} }
  @media (max-width:389px){
    #pgx#pgx .pg-rh .pg-rh-meta .pgx-lad-chip{font-size:11.5px !important}
    #pgx .pg-rh[data-rh="max"] .pg-rh-meta{margin-top:5px;padding-right:0}
    #pgx .pg-rh[data-rh="max"] .pg-rh-meta small{flex-basis:100%}
  }
  #pgx .pg-rh .pg-rh-meta small{flex:0 0 100%;display:block;margin:2px 0 0;font-size:12.5px;line-height:1.6;font-weight:600;color:#fff}
  /* what the bundle includes: a two-column check list, shown on the selected
     tile like the picker block and the tier note */
  #pgx .pg-rh-inc{display:none;width:max-content;max-width:100%;margin:12px auto 0;padding:0;list-style:none;grid-template-columns:auto auto;justify-content:center;gap:7px 24px}
  #pgx .pgx-tile.pgx-sel .pg-rh-inc{display:grid}
  #pgx .pg-rh-inc li{position:relative;padding-left:20px;font-size:13.5px;font-weight:600;color:#F1EDF7;line-height:1.3}
  #pgx .pg-rh-inc li:before{content:"\2713";position:absolute;left:0;top:0;color:#C79BEA;font-weight:800}
  #pgx .pg-rh-inc li b{font-weight:800}
  /* the two cases carry their full names (2026-09-19, "silicone daily case" and "hard shell travel case", as on the Flip SP) on rows of their own under the pairs, so nothing runs past the tile on a 375px phone */
  /* three ticks a side ("checkmarks are not even on both sides", 2026-09-19): the case names stay whole; on phones the columns sit 14px apart and the type steps down so they fit beside their neighbour */
  @media (max-width:389px){ #pgx .pg-rh[data-rh="max"] .pg-rh-inc li{font-size:12px} }
  @media (max-width:419px){ #pgx .pg-rh[data-rh="duo"] .pg-rh-inc li{font-size:11px;padding-left:15px} }
  /* six items, three a side, at every width ("even on both sides"): the
     labels are kept short enough for a 140px column on a 375px phone */
  /* the fallback native picker, only if pgDrop never loads */
  #pgx .pg-rh .pgx-lad-row select.pg-rh-fallback{font-size:12.5px;padding:6px 10px;border-radius:8px;border:1px solid rgba(139,68,190,.5);background:#16101F;color:#fff;font-family:inherit;min-width:160px}
  /* the duo's two pickers wear a small "Console 1 / 2" tag in the tile's
     lavender, so the shopper knows which box is which */
  #pgx .pg-rh .pgx-lad-row .pg-rh-tag{flex:none;width:auto;font-size:12.5px;font-weight:700;color:#C79BEA !important;letter-spacing:.02em;opacity:.82}
  /* two consoles: one width for both tags, so the two pickers line up */
  #pgx .pg-rh[data-rh-qty="2"] .pgx-lad-row .pg-rh-tag,
  #pgx .pg-rh[data-rh="duo"] .pgx-lad-row .pg-rh-tag{width:70px}
  /* the Single Device tile's 1 Console / Duo Pack switch */
  #pgx .pg-rh-qty{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:8px;margin:0 0 10px}
  #pgx .pg-rh-qb{display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:1px;min-height:50px;padding:7px 8px;box-sizing:border-box;
    border:1.5px solid rgba(199,155,234,.4);border-radius:12px;background:rgba(255,255,255,.04);text-align:center;cursor:pointer;
    -webkit-tap-highlight-color:transparent;-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;transition:border-color .15s ease,background-color .15s ease}
  #pgx .pg-rh-qb b{display:block;font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.2;font-weight:800}
  #pgx .pg-rh-qb i{display:block;font-style:normal;font-size:12px;line-height:1.25;font-weight:600;opacity:.75}
  #pgx .pg-rh-qb.on{border-color:#C79BEA;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#9B4BC4,#5B2380);box-shadow:0 10px 22px -14px rgba(155,75,196,.95)}
  #pgx .pg-rh-qb.on i{opacity:.95}
  #pgx .pg-rh-qb:focus-visible{outline:2px solid #C79BEA;outline-offset:2px}
  /* Console 2's row and the Console tags belong to the Duo Pack only. Two
     ids: pg-pick-size sets the rows to display:flex !important at one. */
  #pgx#pgx .pg-rh:not([data-rh-qty="2"]) [data-rh-duo]{display:none !important}
  /* a phone keeps the tag and its picker on ONE line. Two ids: pg-pick-size
     stacks the row and makes the picker full width at one, !important */
  @media (max-width:768px){
    #pgx#pgx .pg-rh .pgx-lad-picks .pgx-lad-row{flex-direction:row !important;align-items:center !important;gap:10px !important;margin-bottom:0 !important}
    #pgx#pgx .pg-rh .pgx-lad-picks .pgx-lad-row + .pgx-lad-row{margin-top:10px !important}
    #pgx#pgx .pg-rh .pgx-lad-picks .pg-drop{flex:1 1 0 !important;width:auto !important;min-width:0 !important}
  }
  /* the line under the name stays on one line down to 375px */
  @media (max-width:380px){
    #pgx .pg-rh .pgx-duo-t small{font-size:12.5px}
  }
  @media (max-width:600px){
    #pgx .pg-rh-inc{gap:6px 14px}
    #pgx .pg-rh-inc li{font-size:12.5px;padding-left:17px;white-space:nowrap}
  }
  /* the three add-on rows under the Single's Add to cart, the Flip SP's rows
     to the pixel (2026-09-19): 44px pictures, 40px on phones */
  #pgx .pg-rh .pg-tadd{gap:11px;padding:7px 10px 7px 9px;border-radius:12px}
  /* three ids: a later section pins every non-frame .pg-tadd img to 30px !important */
  #pgx#pgx#pgx .pg-rh .pg-tadd img{width:44px !important;height:44px !important;border-radius:9px !important}
  #pgx .pg-rh .pg-tadd-t{white-space:normal;font-size:12.5px;line-height:1.25}
  #pgx .pg-rh .pg-tadd-p{font-size:13.5px}
  @media (max-width:600px){
    #pgx .pg-rh .pg-tadd{gap:10px;padding:6px 9px 6px 8px}
    #pgx#pgx#pgx .pg-rh .pg-tadd img{width:40px !important;height:40px !important}
    #pgx .pg-rh .pg-tadd-t{font-size:11.5px}
    #pgx .pg-rh .pg-tadd-p{font-size:12.5px}
  }
</style>

<div class="pg-rh-src" id="pg-rh-src" hidden>
  <div class="pgx-tile pgx-duo pg-rh pgx-sel" data-rh="single" data-rh-qty="1" role="radio" aria-checked="true" tabindex="0">
    <span class="pgx-lad-badge" data-rh-badge></span>
    <span class="pgx-duo-ribbon"></span>
    <div class="pgx-duo-head"><span class="pgx-duo-dot"></span>
      <div class="pgx-duo-t"><b><span data-rh-name>Single Device</span></b></div>
      <div class="pgx-duo-px"><b data-rh-now></b><s data-rh-was></s><span class="pgx-lad-chip pgx-each"></span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-rh-meta"><span class="pgx-lad-chip" data-rh-chip>64GB &middot; 15,000+ Games</span><small data-rh-sub>Landscape grip, dual sticks, plays on your TV</small></div>
    <div class="pgx-lad-picks">
      <div class="pg-rh-qty" role="radiogroup" aria-label="How many consoles">
        <span class="pg-rh-qb on" role="radio" aria-checked="true" tabindex="0" data-rh-qb="1"><b>1 Console</b><i data-rh-q1></i></span>
        <span class="pg-rh-qb" role="radio" aria-checked="false" tabindex="0" data-rh-qb="2"><b>Duo Pack</b><i data-rh-q2></i></span>
      </div>
      <div class="pgx-lad-row" data-rh-row="1"><span class="pg-rh-tag" data-rh-tag1>Color</span></div>
      <div class="pgx-lad-row" data-rh-row="2" data-rh-duo><span class="pg-rh-tag">Console 2</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="pgx-tier-note" data-rh-note><b>One R36H Pro (64GB)</b> with 15,000+ games preloaded, plus an extra <b>5% off</b> at checkout.</div>
    <!-- the three add-on rows (silicone daily case, hard shell travel case,
         screen protector): the JS re-seats them under the phone Add to cart
         button and re-words / re-prices them when the Duo Pack switch moves -->
    {%- if add_sil and add_sil.available -%}
    <div class="pg-tadd" role="checkbox" aria-checked="false" tabindex="0" data-rh-add="silicone" data-rh-add-id="{{ add_sil.selected_or_first_available_variant.id }}"><span class="pg-tadd-ck" aria-hidden="true"></span><img alt="" src="{{ add_sil.featured_image | image_url: width: 160 }}"><span class="pg-tadd-t">Add Silicone Daily Case</span><span class="pg-tadd-p"><s>{{ add_sil.compare_at_price | default: add_sil.price | money }}</s><b>{{ add_sil.price | money }}</b></span></div>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if add_hard and add_hard.available -%}
    <div class="pg-tadd" role="checkbox" aria-checked="false" tabindex="0" data-rh-add="hardshell" data-rh-add-id="{{ add_hard.selected_or_first_available_variant.id }}"><span class="pg-tadd-ck" aria-hidden="true"></span><img alt="" src="{{ add_hard.featured_image | image_url: width: 160 }}"><span class="pg-tadd-t">Add Hard Shell Travel Case</span><span class="pg-tadd-p"><s>{{ add_hard.compare_at_price | default: add_hard.price | money }}</s><b>{{ add_hard.price | money }}</b></span></div>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if add_prot and add_prot.available -%}
    <div class="pg-tadd" role="checkbox" aria-checked="false" tabindex="0" data-rh-add="protector" data-rh-add-id="{{ add_prot.selected_or_first_available_variant.id }}"><span class="pg-tadd-ck" aria-hidden="true"></span><img alt="" src="{{ add_prot.featured_image | image_url: width: 160 }}"><span class="pg-tadd-t">Add Screen Protector</span><span class="pg-tadd-p"><s>{{ add_prot.compare_at_price | default: add_prot.price | money }}</s><b>{{ add_prot.price | money }}</b></span></div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>

  <div class="pgx-tile pgx-duo pg-rh" data-rh="max" role="radio" aria-checked="false" tabindex="0">
    <span class="pgx-lad-badge" data-rh-badge></span>
    <span class="pgx-duo-ribbon"></span>
    <div class="pgx-duo-head"><span class="pgx-duo-dot"></span>
      <div class="pgx-duo-t"><b>Max Bundle</b></div>
      <div class="pgx-duo-px"><b data-rh-now></b><s data-rh-was></s><span class="pgx-lad-chip pgx-each"></span></div>
    </div>
      <div class="pg-rh-meta"><span class="pgx-lad-chip">128GB &middot; 20K Games + 3 Accessories</span><small>One console plus the full protection kit</small></div>
    <div class="pgx-lad-picks"><div class="pgx-lad-row" data-rh-row="1"><span class="pg-rh-tag">Color</span></div></div>
    <ul class="pg-rh-inc">
      <li><b>128GB</b> Storage</li>
      <li><b>20K</b> Games</li>
      <li>Screen Protector</li>
      <li>USB-C Cable</li>
      <li>Silicone Daily Case</li>
      <li>Hard Shell Travel Case</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="pgx-tier-note">Saves <b data-rh-savings></b> vs buying separately, plus an extra <b>5% off</b> at checkout.</div>
  </div>

  <div class="pgx-tile pgx-duo pg-rh" data-rh="duo" role="radio" aria-checked="false" tabindex="0">
    <span class="pgx-lad-badge" data-rh-badge></span>
    <span class="pgx-duo-ribbon"></span>
    <div class="pgx-duo-head"><span class="pgx-duo-dot"></span>
      <div class="pgx-duo-t"><b>Duo Max Bundle</b></div>
      <div class="pgx-duo-px"><b data-rh-now></b><s data-rh-was></s><span class="pgx-lad-chip pgx-each" data-rh-each></span></div>
    </div>
      <div class="pg-rh-meta"><span class="pgx-lad-chip">2X 128GB &middot; 20K Games + 2X 3 Accessories</span><small>Two consoles, two protection kits</small></div>
    <div class="pgx-lad-picks">
      <div class="pgx-lad-row" data-rh-row="1"><span class="pg-rh-tag">Console 1</span></div>
      <div class="pgx-lad-row" data-rh-row="2"><span class="pg-rh-tag">Console 2</span></div>
    </div>
    <ul class="pg-rh-inc">
      <li><b>2X</b> 128GB Storage</li>
      <li><b>2X</b> 20K Games</li>
      <li><b>2X</b> Screen Protector</li>
      <li><b>2X</b> USB-C Cable</li>
      <li><b>2X</b> Silicone Daily Case</li>
      <li><b>2X</b> Hard Shell Travel Case</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="pgx-tier-note"><b>Everything in the Max Bundle, twice.</b> Pick a color for each console, plus an extra <b>5% off</b> at checkout.</div>
  </div>
</div>

<script type="application/json" id="pg-rh-data">
{"duoOff":{{ section.settings.duo_off | default: '5.00' | times: 100 | round }},"duoMaxOff":{{ section.settings.duomax_off | default: '30.00' | times: 100 | round }},"kit":{"id":{{ add_kit.selected_or_first_available_variant.id | default: 0 }},"p":{{ add_kit.price | default: 0 }}},"img0":{{ p.featured_image | image_url: width: 200 | json }},"colors":[{%- if color_opt != blank -%}{%- for value in color_opt.values -%}{{ value | json }}{%- unless forloop.last -%},{%- endunless -%}{%- endfor -%}{%- endif -%}],"variants":[{%- for v in p.variants -%}{"id":{{ v.id }},"b":{{ v.option1 | json }},"c":{{ v.option2 | json }},"c2":{{ v.option3 | default: 'None' | json }},"p":{{ v.price }},"cap":{{ v.compare_at_price | default: 0 }},"av":{{ v.available | json }},"img":{% if v.featured_image %}{{ v.featured_image | image_url: width: 200 | json }}{% else %}""{% endif %},"big":{% if v.featured_image %}{{ v.featured_image | image_url: width: 1400 | json }}{% else %}""{% endif %}}{%- unless forloop.last -%},{%- endunless -%}{%- endfor -%}],"addons":{"silicone":{"id":{{ add_sil.selected_or_first_available_variant.id | default: 0 }},"p":{{ add_sil.price | default: 0 }},"cap":{{ add_sil.compare_at_price | default: 0 }},"img":{{ add_sil.featured_image | image_url: width: 160 | json }}},"hardshell":{"id":{{ add_hard.selected_or_first_available_variant.id | default: 0 }},"p":{{ add_hard.price | default: 0 }},"cap":{{ add_hard.compare_at_price | default: 0 }},"img":{{ add_hard.featured_image | image_url: width: 160 | json }}},"protector":{"id":{{ add_prot.selected_or_first_available_variant.id | default: 0 }},"p":{{ add_prot.price | default: 0 }},"cap":{{ add_prot.compare_at_price | default: 0 }},"img":{{ add_prot.featured_image | image_url: width: 160 | json }}}}}
</script>

<script>
(function(){
  if (window.pgR36hTiles) return; window.pgR36hTiles = 1;
  /* claimed before the footer group runs: see the note at the top */
  window.pgLadder = 1;
  window.pgDuo = 1;

  var dataEl = document.getElementById('pg-rh-data');
  if (!dataEl) return;
  var DATA; try { DATA = JSON.parse(dataEl.textContent); } catch (e){ return; }
  var VARS = DATA.variants || [];
  if (!VARS.length) return;
  /* cents off EACH console of a Duo Pack of singles: mirrors the admin's
     automatic discount "R36H Pro - Duo Pack Savings" (see the note at the top) */
  var DUO_OFF = Math.max(0, parseInt(DATA.duoOff, 10) || 0);
  /* cents off EACH Max Bundle console of a Duo Max (2026-09-21): mirrors the
     admin's automatic discount "R36H Pro - Duo Max Savings" ($30.00 off
     each, two or more), the same way DUO_OFF mirrors the Duo Pack's */
  var DUOMAX_OFF = Math.max(0, parseInt(DATA.duoMaxOff, 10) || 0);
  /* the Protection Kit, one variant: posted beside every Max console, free at the till ("R36H Pro - Max Kit Free") */
  var KIT = DATA.kit || {};
  /* the discount is a fixed amount in the shop's currency and the till
     converts it. Seen in CAD on 2026-09-17: the tile took a flat $10.00 off
     $214.00 where checkout takes about $14.20. The variant prices here are
     already in the shopper's currency, so the amount is scaled by the same
     rate. Shopify rounds converted amounts its own way, so outside the shop
     currency this can still differ from the till by a few cents. */
  (function(){
    var r = window.Shopify && Shopify.currency && parseFloat(Shopify.currency.rate);
    if (r && r > 0 && r !== 1){ DUO_OFF = Math.round(DUO_OFF * r); DUOMAX_OFF = Math.round(DUOMAX_OFF * r); }
  })();
  var COLORS = (DATA.colors && DATA.colors.length) ? DATA.colors : [VARS[0].c];
  var DEFAULT_COLOR = COLORS[0];

  var BUNDLE = {single: 'Single Device (64GB)', max: 'Max Bundle (128GB)', duo: 'Duo Max Bundle (2x 128GB)'};
  var LABEL = {single: '', max: 'MOST POPULAR', duo: 'BEST DEAL'};

  function money(c){ return '$' + (c / 100).toFixed(2); }
  function pct(v){ return v && v.cap > v.p ? Math.floor((v.cap - v.p) / v.cap * 100) : 0; }

  /* one photo per colour: the first variant of that colour with its own image */
  var IMG = {}, BIG = {};
  VARS.forEach(function(v){ if (v.img && !IMG[v.c]) IMG[v.c] = v.img; if (v.big && !BIG[v.c]) BIG[v.c] = v.big; });
  var OPTS = COLORS.map(function(c){ return {id: c, t: c, img: IMG[c] || DATA.img0 || ''}; });

  /* ---------------- the pickers ---------------- */

  /* the picker in a row: pgDrop's widget (pgValue()) or the fallback select */
  function pickerOf(row){ return row.querySelector('.pg-drop, select.pg-rh-fallback'); }
  function valueOf(el){
    if (!el) return DEFAULT_COLOR;
    if (typeof el.pgValue === 'function') return String(el.pgValue());
    return el.value || DEFAULT_COLOR;
  }
  var fallbackAt = Date.now() + 4000;   /* pgDrop has this long to show up */
  function buildPickers(){
    var pending = false;
    tiles().forEach(function(tile){
      tile.querySelectorAll('[data-rh-row]').forEach(function(row){
        if (pickerOf(row)) return;
        if (typeof window.pgDrop === 'function'){
          row.appendChild(window.pgDrop(OPTS, DEFAULT_COLOR, function(){ paint(tile); }));
        } else if (Date.now() > fallbackAt){
          var s = document.createElement('select');
          s.className = 'pg-rh-fallback';
          s.setAttribute('aria-label', 'Color');
          OPTS.forEach(function(o){ var op = document.createElement('option'); op.value = o.id; op.textContent = o.t; s.appendChild(op); });
          s.addEventListener('click', function(e){ e.stopPropagation(); });
          s.addEventListener('change', function(){ paint(tile); });
          row.appendChild(s);
        } else {
          pending = true;
        }
      });
    });
    return !pending;
  }

  function pick(tile){
    var rows = tile.querySelectorAll('[data-rh-row]');
    var c1 = rows[0] ? valueOf(pickerOf(rows[0])) : DEFAULT_COLOR;
    var c2 = rows[1] ? valueOf(pickerOf(rows[1])) : 'None';
    return {c1: c1, c2: c2};
  }
  function find(b, c1, c2){
    var hit = null;
    VARS.forEach(function(v){ if (!hit && v.b === b && v.c === c1 && v.c2 === c2) hit = v; });
    return hit;
  }
  function firstOf(b){
    var hit = null;
    VARS.forEach(function(v){ if (!hit && v.b === b) hit = v; });   /* the first of the tier, never nothing */
    return hit;
  }
  /* the Single Device tile switched to Duo Pack */
  function isPair(tile){ return tile.getAttribute('data-rh') === 'single' && tile.getAttribute('data-rh-qty') === '2'; }
  /* WHAT THE TILE SELLS RIGHT NOW: one variant, or, for a Duo Pack of singles,
     the two Single Device variants that were picked. A single's variants all
     carry "None" as their second colour, so its Console 2 picker names a
     second SINGLE, never a c2. */
  function linesFor(tile){
    var kind = tile.getAttribute('data-rh'), k = pick(tile), b = BUNDLE[kind];
    if (kind === 'single'){
      var one = find(b, k.c1, 'None') || firstOf(b);
      if (!one) return [];
      if (!isPair(tile)) return [one];
      return [one, find(b, k.c2, 'None') || one];
    }
    /* THE DUO MAX IS TWO MAX BUNDLE LINES (2026-09-21, AutoDS fulfils one
       supplier SKU per cart line, so the one-variant Duo Max is gone): the
       Max Bundle variant of each picked colour, one line of two when they
       match. The admin's "R36H Pro - Duo Max Savings" takes DUOMAX_OFF off
       each from two up; the kit rides as a free line of its own (Add to cart). */
    if (kind === 'duo'){
      var m1 = find(BUNDLE.max, k.c1, 'None') || firstOf(BUNDLE.max);
      if (!m1) return [];
      return [m1, find(BUNDLE.max, k.c2, 'None') || m1];
    }
    var v = find(b, k.c1, 'None') || firstOf(b);
    return v ? [v] : [];
  }

  /* the words on the Single Device tile, for one console and for two */
  var COPY = {
    one: {name: 'Single Device', chip: '64GB \u00b7 15,000+ Games', sub: 'Landscape grip, dual sticks, plays on your TV', tag: 'Color',
      note: '<b>One R36H Pro (64GB)</b> with 15,000+ games preloaded, plus an extra <b>5% off</b> at checkout.'},
    two: {name: 'Duo Pack', chip: '2X 64GB \u00b7 15,000+ Games', sub: 'One for you, one to gift', tag: 'Console 1',
      note: '<b>Two R36H Pro (64GB)</b> with 15,000+ games each, plus an extra <b>5% off</b> at checkout.'}
  };
  var ADDONS = DATA.addons || {};
  /* the words on the add-on rows, for one console and for two (the Duo Pack
     offers two of each, as on the Flip SP) */
  var ADD_COPY = {
    silicone: {one: 'Add Silicone Daily Case', two: 'Add 2 Silicone Daily Cases'},
    hardshell: {one: 'Add Hard Shell Travel Case', two: 'Add 2 Hard Shell Travel Cases'},
    protector: {one: 'Add Screen Protector', two: 'Add 2 Screen Protectors'}
  };
  function addRows(tile){ return Array.prototype.slice.call(tile.querySelectorAll('[data-rh-add]')); }
  /* the add-on rows: worded and priced for the number of consoles in the tile */
  function dressAddons(tile, n){
    addRows(tile).forEach(function(row){
      var key = row.getAttribute('data-rh-add'), a = ADDONS[key], w = ADD_COPY[key];
      if (!a || !w) return;
      setText(row.querySelector('.pg-tadd-t'), n > 1 ? w.two : w.one);
      setText(row.querySelector('.pg-tadd-p s'), money((a.cap > a.p ? a.cap : a.p) * n));
      setText(row.querySelector('.pg-tadd-p b'), money(a.p * n));
    });
  }
  /* THE ROWS SIT UNDER THE ADD TO CART BUTTON, ALWAYS. pg-r36s-mobile appends
     its in-tile .pg-r36-atc button to the tile on phones; the rows are
     re-seated right after it on every paint, idempotently, in their own
     order. On desktop there is no button and they stay at the end of the
     tile, after the tier note. */
  function seatAddons(tile){
    var atcB = tile.querySelector('.pg-r36-atc');
    if (!atcB || atcB.parentNode !== tile) return;
    var after = atcB;
    addRows(tile).forEach(function(row){
      if (row.parentNode === tile && (after.compareDocumentPosition(row) & 2)) tile.insertBefore(row, after.nextSibling);
      after = row;
    });
  }
  /* what the lines cost together: a Duo Pack of singles has the discount off each */
  function priceOf(tile, lines){
    var p = 0;
    lines.forEach(function(v){ p += v.p; });
    if (isPair(tile)) p -= Math.min(p, DUO_OFF * lines.length);
    if (tile.getAttribute('data-rh') === 'duo') p -= Math.min(p, DUOMAX_OFF * lines.length);
    return p;
  }
  function setText(el, txt){ if (el && el.textContent !== txt) el.textContent = txt; }
  function dress(tile, lines){
    var c = isPair(tile) ? COPY.two : COPY.one;
    setText(tile.querySelector('[data-rh-name]'), c.name);
    setText(tile.querySelector('[data-rh-chip]'), c.chip);
    setText(tile.querySelector('[data-rh-sub]'), c.sub);
    setText(tile.querySelector('[data-rh-tag1]'), c.tag);
    var a = lines[0], z = lines[1] || lines[0];
    var two = Math.max(0, a.p + z.p - DUO_OFF * 2);
    var note = tile.querySelector('[data-rh-note]');
    if (note && note.pgCopy !== c.note){ note.pgCopy = c.note; note.innerHTML = c.note; }
    /* the switch prices itself from the colours picked */
    setText(tile.querySelector('[data-rh-q1]'), money(a.p));
    setText(tile.querySelector('[data-rh-q2]'), '2 for ' + money(two));
    dressAddons(tile, lines.length);
    seatAddons(tile);
  }
  function setQty(tile, q){
    tile.setAttribute('data-rh-qty', q === 2 ? '2' : '1');
    tile.querySelectorAll('[data-rh-qb]').forEach(function(b){
      var on = b.getAttribute('data-rh-qb') === String(q);
      b.classList.toggle('on', on);
      b.setAttribute('aria-checked', on ? 'true' : 'false');
    });
    paint(tile);
  }

  function paint(tile){
    var lines = linesFor(tile); if (!lines.length) return;
    var kind = tile.getAttribute('data-rh');
    /* a Duo Pack of singles is priced, struck and badged on the sum of its
       two, less the Duo discount the till takes off each */
    var p = priceOf(tile, lines), cap = 0;
    lines.forEach(function(v){ cap += (v.cap > v.p ? v.cap : v.p); });
    var now = tile.querySelector('[data-rh-now]'), was = tile.querySelector('[data-rh-was]'), badge = tile.querySelector('[data-rh-badge]');
    setText(now, money(p));
    setText(was, cap > p ? money(cap) : '');
    var pc = pct({p: p, cap: cap});
    var bt = pc > 0 ? ((LABEL[kind] ? LABEL[kind] + ' · ' : '') + 'SAVE ' + pc + '%') : '';
    if (badge){
      if (badge.textContent !== bt) badge.textContent = bt;
      badge.style.display = bt ? '' : 'none';
    }
    var each = tile.querySelector('[data-rh-each]');
    if (each) setText(each, money(Math.ceil(p / 2)) + ' each');
    var sav = tile.querySelector('[data-rh-savings]');
    if (sav && cap > p) setText(sav, money(cap - p));
    if (kind === 'single') dress(tile, lines);
  }

  function tiles(){ return Array.prototype.slice.call(document.querySelectorAll('#pgx .pgx-buy > .pgx-tile.pg-rh')); }
  function selected(){ return document.querySelector('#pgx .pgx-buy > .pgx-tile.pg-rh.pgx-sel'); }

  function select(tile){
    document.querySelectorAll('#pgx .pgx-tile.pgx-sel').forEach(function(x){ x.classList.remove('pgx-sel'); x.setAttribute('aria-checked', 'false'); });
    tile.classList.add('pgx-sel');
    tile.setAttribute('aria-checked', 'true');
  }

  /* seat the tiles in pg-landing's buy column, after its (hidden) native
     single tile, so pg-r36s-mobile (in-tile Add to cart, phone ordering),
     pg-sellout-last and pg-offer-copy find them where they expect tiles */
  function seat(){
    var src = document.getElementById('pg-rh-src');
    var buy = document.querySelector('#pgx .pgx-buy');
    if (!src || !buy) return false;
    var pgx = document.getElementById('pgx');
    if (pgx && !pgx.hasAttribute('data-pg-tiernotes')) pgx.setAttribute('data-pg-tiernotes', '1');
    var native = buy.querySelector(':scope > .pgx-tile[data-pgx-tile="single"]');
    var anchor = native ? native.nextSibling : (buy.querySelector('#pgx-atc') || null);
    var moved = false;
    Array.prototype.slice.call(src.querySelectorAll('.pg-rh')).forEach(function(t){
      buy.insertBefore(t, anchor);
      moved = true;
      t.addEventListener('click', function(){ select(t); });
      t.addEventListener('keydown', function(e){ if (e.key === ' ' || e.key === 'Enter'){ e.preventDefault(); select(t); } });
      t.querySelectorAll('[data-rh-qb]').forEach(function(b){
        var q = b.getAttribute('data-rh-qb') === '2' ? 2 : 1;
        b.addEventListener('click', function(){ setQty(t, q); });
        b.addEventListener('keydown', function(e){
          if (e.key !== ' ' && e.key !== 'Enter') return;
          e.preventDefault(); e.stopPropagation();
          select(t); setQty(t, q);
        });
      });
      paint(t);
    });
    if (native) { native.classList.remove('pgx-sel'); native.setAttribute('aria-checked', 'false'); }
    /* the "Bundle & Save" heading pgDuo draws over the R36S tiles (pg-mobile
       hides pg-landing's own divider on every page) */
    var firstTile = buy.querySelector(':scope > .pgx-tile.pg-rh');
    if (moved && firstTile && !buy.querySelector('.pgx-bs')){
      var bs = document.createElement('div');
      bs.className = 'pgx-bs';
      bs.innerHTML = '<span>Bundle &amp; Save</span>';
      buy.insertBefore(bs, firstTile);
    }
    return moved;
  }

  /* ONE OWNER FOR ADD TO CART. Window, capture phase: first node in the
     propagation path, so it runs before pg-landing's handler on #pgx-atc and
     before every document-level listener in the footer group. */
  /* THE ADD-ON ROWS TOGGLE. Capture phase and stopPropagation: a click on a
     row must not fall through to the tile's own click handler chain twice,
     and must never reach the pickers. Toggling still SELECTS the tile first
     if it was not. Enter and Space do what a click does. */
  document.addEventListener('click', function(e){
    var row = e.target && e.target.closest && e.target.closest('#pgx .pg-rh .pg-tadd');
    if (!row) return;
    e.stopPropagation();
    var tile = row.closest('.pg-rh');
    if (tile && !tile.classList.contains('pgx-sel')) select(tile);
    var on = !row.classList.contains('on');
    row.classList.toggle('on', on);
    row.setAttribute('aria-checked', on ? 'true' : 'false');
  }, true);
  document.addEventListener('keydown', function(e){
    if (e.key !== ' ' && e.key !== 'Enter') return;
    var row = e.target && e.target.closest && e.target.closest('#pgx .pg-rh .pg-tadd');
    if (!row) return;
    e.preventDefault();
    e.stopPropagation();
    row.click();
  }, true);

  var busy = false;
  window.addEventListener('click', function(e){
    if (!e.target || !e.target.closest) return;
    var atc = e.target.closest('.pgx-atc');
    if (!atc) return;
    var tile = selected();
    if (!tile) return;
    e.preventDefault();
    e.stopPropagation();
    if (e.stopImmediatePropagation) e.stopImmediatePropagation();
    if (busy) return;
    var lines = linesFor(tile);
    var err = document.getElementById('pgx-err');
    if (!lines.length) return;
    /* one line of two when both consoles are the same colour */
    var items = [];
    lines.forEach(function(v){
      var hit = null;
      items.forEach(function(it){ if (it.id === v.id) hit = it; });
      if (hit) hit.quantity += 1; else items.push({id: v.id, quantity: 1});
    });
    /* each add-on that was ticked, one per console */
    addRows(tile).forEach(function(row){
      if (!row.classList.contains('on')) return;
      var id = parseInt(row.getAttribute('data-rh-add-id'), 10);
      if (id > 0) items.push({id: id, quantity: lines.length});
    });
    /* THE KIT IS A LINE OF ITS OWN (2026-09-21, AutoDS: one supplier SKU per
       cart line, and the supplier ships the three accessories as one item).
       The Max and the Duo Max post the Protection Kit at quantity = the
       number of consoles; the admin's "R36H Pro - Max Kit Free" makes it free
       beside a Max console, so the console line carries the whole price and
       the kit row reads FREE. */
    var kindNow = tile.getAttribute('data-rh');
    if ((kindNow === 'max' || kindNow === 'duo') && KIT.id > 0) items.push({id: KIT.id, quantity: lines.length});
    if (lines.some(function(v){ return !v.av; })){
      if (err){ err.textContent = 'That configuration is sold out right now. Try another color.'; err.style.display = 'block'; }
      return;
    }
    busy = true;
    var lbl = atc.querySelector('span'), old = lbl ? lbl.textContent : '';
    if (lbl) lbl.textContent = 'Adding...';
    if (err) err.style.display = 'none';
    fetch('/cart/add.js', {
      method: 'POST',
      headers: {'Content-Type': 'application/json'},
      credentials: 'same-origin',
      body: JSON.stringify({items: items})
    }).then(function(r){
      busy = false;
      if (lbl) lbl.textContent = old || 'Add to cart';
      if (!r.ok) throw new Error('add failed');
      if (window.pgOpenCart) { window.pgOpenCart(); } else { window.location.href = '/cart'; }
    }).catch(function(){
      busy = false;
      if (lbl) lbl.textContent = old || 'Add to cart';
      if (err){ err.textContent = 'Could not add to cart. Please try again.'; err.style.display = 'block'; }
    });
  }, true);

  /* the name of the colour whose render the big photo is showing, as a pill
     on the photo; hidden on any photo that is not a colour render */
  function fileOf(u){ u = String(u || '').split('?')[0]; u = u.substring(u.lastIndexOf('/') + 1); return u.replace(/_(\d+x\d*|x\d+)(@\dx)?(?=\.[a-z]+$)/i, '').toLowerCase(); }
  function colourOf(src){
    var file = fileOf(src);
    if (!file) return '';
    for (var c in BIG){ if (BIG[c] && fileOf(BIG[c]) === file) return c; }
    return '';
  }
  function capOn(box, img){
    var cap = box.querySelector(':scope > .pg-rh-hcap');
    if (!cap){ cap = document.createElement('span'); cap.className = 'pg-rh-hcap'; cap.setAttribute('aria-hidden', 'true'); box.appendChild(cap); }
    var name = colourOf(img.currentSrc || img.getAttribute('src'));
    if (cap.textContent !== name) cap.textContent = name;
    cap.classList.toggle('on', !!name);
  }
  function heroCap(){
    var img = document.getElementById('pgx-hero-img');
    if (img && img.parentNode) capOn(img.parentNode, img);
    /* the phone carousel: one pill per slide */
    document.querySelectorAll('#pgx .pgx-thumbs > button').forEach(function(b){
      var im = b.querySelector('img');
      if (im) capOn(b, im);
    });
  }
  function boot(){
    var seated = seat();
    setInterval(function(){ try { heroCap(); } catch (e){} }, 300);
    var n = 0;
    var t = setInterval(function(){
      if (!seated) seated = seat();
      var done = seated && buildPickers();
      if (done && seated){ tiles().forEach(paint); }
      if ((done && seated) || ++n > 40) clearInterval(t);
    }, 200);
    if (seated) buildPickers();
    /* prices settle on a slow beat too, in case another script rebuilds a
       tile's text; a picker lost to a rebuild is put back the same way */
    setInterval(function(){ buildPickers(); tiles().forEach(paint); }, 2500);
  }
  if (document.readyState === 'loading') document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', boot); else boot();
})();
</script>
